invariant: INV-27
file: quic_aes.h
catches: test/lint-quic-partition.sh
reason: a new type lands at the top of quic_aes.h, above the
  #ifdef CH_TRANSPORT_QUIC the rest of the file sits under, so a
  TLS build compiles a declaration from a file the mode owns.
  The file still carries the prefix and still preprocesses, so
  nothing that reads names or builds objects notices. The lint
  preprocesses the file without the define and sees the
  declaration, so it objects.

--- old
#ifndef CH_QUIC_AES_H
#define CH_QUIC_AES_H
#ifdef CH_TRANSPORT_QUIC
--- new
#ifndef CH_QUIC_AES_H
#define CH_QUIC_AES_H

// One AES-128 block, written above the transport guard.
typedef struct {
    unsigned char b[16];
} aes_block;

#ifdef CH_TRANSPORT_QUIC
